finally had the screws and metals removed from leg, feels better, seems fine, but now enjoying a week-long (so far) of pretty bad case of stomach cramps, man will the summer adventures never end?, also solar eclipse it's just a week away, excited

as for progress in the z80 front, i decided that just studying other people's code leaves too many 'proofs are left as exercises for the reader', so went ahead to download some books and references on the z80, still not a lot of tangible src code was made but 'z80 assembly language programming' by leventhal is a comprehensive guide that already solved lots of nebulous concepts encountered (differences between hl or bc? etc), and more importantly, lots and of lots of exercises starting from zero to the very hard, designed to help you achieve proficiency with the z80 and assembler, i'm weeding through them, also it demonstrates (again) that the youtube tutorial industry archived little teaching stuff, seems nothing beats 700-pagebook of computer literature from 1979
